(S, "Who negotiated the Durand Line for British India?", ["Lord Curzon", "Lord Mountbatten", "Sir Mortimer Durand", "Lord Dalhousie"], 2, "Sir Mortimer Durand, the Foreign Secretary of British India, negotiated the line with Amir Abdur Rahman Khan in 1893. The line is named after him.", "The Afghan ruler at that time was Amir Abdur Rahman Khan.", [4377]),
